---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Is the photographer a woman?",
    a: "Yes. Every session is just you and me, no assistant, no one else in the room. I shoot everything myself.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do you photograph plus sized women?",
    a: "Hell yes. Every body deserves to be seen, celebrated, and photographed with love. I work with women of all shapes and sizes, and I'll guide you through every step so you feel confident, beautiful, and sexy. You don't need to change a thing to deserve stunning photos.",
  },
  {
    q: "What age of women do you work with?",
    a: "All of them. I've photographed women in their twenties discovering their confidence, women in their forties reclaiming it, and women in their sixties celebrating it. Boudoir isn't about being a certain age, it's about capturing your energy, your story, and the way you feel in your skin, right now.",
  },
  {
    q: "I have scars, or I've had surgery. Is that a problem?",
    a: "No. I have photographed women with surgical scars, with burns, and in the weeks before a mastectomy so they had something of themselves from before. A body that has been through something is not a problem to be worked around, and you will not have to explain it to me. Tell me beforehand what you would like brought forward and what you would rather I keep out of frame, and that is exactly what I will do.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I bring a support person?",
    a: "If you want to bring a friend along for support, that's totally fine, as long as they're ready to match your energy and bring good vibes only. This is your time to shine, and I'm here to make sure it feels exactly that.",
  },
  {
    q: "I don't know how to pose! Will I look awkward in the photos?",
    a: "You don't need to know a single pose before you arrive, that's my job. I'll guide you through everything, from the way you hold your hands to the little details that make a big difference, and I'll demonstrate the poses myself so you're never left wondering what to do.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will my photos be shared online?",
    a: "No, not unless you say it's okay. Your privacy is incredibly important to me, and I'll never share your images anywhere without your permission — this is your session, your body, your call. I also delete my copies after I've delivered your final images, so please back up several copies for yourself, as I won't have them if you misplace your copy.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I buy a session as a gift?",
    a: [
      "Yes, I do gift certificates, and it is one of the most common ways sessions get booked. Friends buy them for a friend's milestone birthday, and plenty of men buy one for their wife as a birthday or Valentine's gift.",
      "You get in touch first and we have a proper conversation about who she is and what kind of shoot would suit her. I then send you a digital voucher to pass on. It tells her that somebody who loves her has given her the gift of a boudoir shoot, and it sets out how long her session is and how many images she gets. It does not show the price, so she never sees what you spent.",
      "When she is ready she gives me a call, and that conversation is just with her. We talk through the kind of photos she wants, what to bring, and exactly how the day will run, because knowing what happens is what settles the nerves.",
      "She has three months to use it, and that is on purpose. Left open ended, a lot of women put it off, usually waiting until they have lost weight or until some better version of themselves turns up. She does not need to be any different to do this. Three months is a gentle push to actually take the time for herself.",
    ],
  },
  {
    q: "Do you do bridal boudoir?",
    a: "Yes, and often. It is one of the most common reasons women book, usually as a gift for a partner before the wedding, and just as often as something for themselves. Get in touch early so we can find a date that leaves you plenty of room before the day.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I book a session?",
    a: "Tell me about the shoot you're dreaming of. Boudoir photography is incredibly personal — no two shoots are the same, because no two people are. Whatever you're imagining, I'd love to hear about it. Fill out the contact form and share a little about who you are and what you're hoping for, there's no pressure and no right answers. Once I've got your details, I'll be in touch for a quick, friendly chat to talk through the experience, answer any questions, and plan what happens next.",
  },
  {
    q: "What do I wear?",
    a: "Whatever feels like you. That might mean a lacy lingerie set, your favourite white shirt, a comfy oversized jumper, or nothing at all — nude is a popular option. Bring it all and we'll talk through what works best once you're here. Some clients show up a bit nervous, that's totally normal, but by the end of the session they're owning it. After you get in touch I'll ask if you'd like me to call you so we can talk it all through and get you fully prepared.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does my session include?",
    a: "What's included depends on the package you choose, so the best place to start is the pricing page, where everything is laid out clearly. No matter which package you go for, you'll get expert guidance, a relaxed and supportive environment, and images that reflect your beauty and energy. If you're unsure which option is right for you, just reach out and I'm happy to talk it through.",
  },
  {
    q: "How far in advance should I book?",
    a: "If you have a deadline in mind, book at least four weeks in advance so there's plenty of time for your shoot and final images. My calendar fills up fast, so the sooner you get in touch, the better.",
  },
  {
    q: "When do I pay for my session?",
    a: "Full payment is required at the time of booking to secure your shoot. I hold that time just for you, and often turn away other clients to keep your spot open, so payments are non-refundable. If you need to reschedule and give enough notice, I'll always do my best to find a new time that works.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long does a boudoir shoot really take?",
    a: "The packages list 1.5, 2.5 or unlimited hours, but in practice I usually take close to double that. Before we shoot, we talk through the kind of photos you want, any injuries or limitations, and how your outfits work with them. Then we do a few practice poses so you know how I like to guide you before the camera comes out properly.",
  },
  {
    q: "How many shoots do you do in a day?",
    a: "Just one. That's deliberate, so you get my full attention and I'm never rushing you through it.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do you photograph men?",
    a: "I've been working exclusively with women since the beginning of my photography journey. My services are offered solely to women, with the exception of couples sessions.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do you travel?",
    a: "Most of my shoots are in my studio, but I'm open to travelling if that will make you more comfortable.",
  },
  {
    q: "What's your background as a photographer?",
    a: "I hold a master's in photography, focused specifically on posing and lighting. A lot of bad boudoir photos come down to getting those two things wrong, not the person in front of the camera.",
  },
];

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      "@type": "Answer",
      text: Array.isArray(f.a) ? f.a.join(" ") : f.a,
    },
  })),
};
---

<Base
  title="Boudoir Photography FAQs | Auckland"
  description="Answers to the questions clients ask most before their Auckland boudoir photography session — what to wear, how sessions work, privacy, and booking."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 text-center">
    <h1 class="text-4xl text-boudoir-ink md:text-5xl">FAQs</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <div class="divide-y divide-boudoir-cream">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="group py-5">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-left font-semibold text-boudoir-ink">
            <span>{faq.q}</span>
            <span class="shrink-0 text-xl text-boudoir-pink transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-boudoir-muted">
            {(Array.isArray(faq.a) ? faq.a : [faq.a]).map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 text-center">
      <p class="text-boudoir-muted">Still have a question?</p>
      <a
        href="/contact-boudoir-photography-auckland"
        class="mt-4 inline-block border-2 border-boudoir-pink px-6 py-3 text-boudoir-pink hover:bg-boudoir-pink hover:text-boudoir-ink"
      >
        Contact me today
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
